#!/bin/sh
# usb-moded races the dwc3 UDC during early boot (its first mtp bind hits
# "No such device" and it silently falls back to charging_only, 18d1:0afe,
# which enumerates as a dead mass-storage stub on the host). Once the system
# is settled the UDC is stable, so retry the mode selection.
sleep 12
g=/sys/kernel/config/usb_gadget/g1
udc=$(cat "$g"/UDC 2>/dev/null)
pid=$(cat "$g"/idProduct 2>/dev/null)
echo "ut-usb-retry: state UDC='$udc' idProduct='$pid'"
if [ "$pid" = "0x6860" ] && [ -n "$udc" ]; then
    echo "ut-usb-retry: mtp gadget already up, nothing to do"
    exit 0
fi
# unbind whatever half-configured gadget is there and let usb-moded redo it
echo "" > "$g"/UDC 2>/dev/null
systemctl restart usb-moded
sleep 4
command -v usb-moded-util >/dev/null && usb-moded-util -s mtp 2>/dev/null
sleep 3
echo "ut-usb-retry: after retry UDC='$(cat "$g"/UDC 2>/dev/null)' idProduct='$(cat "$g"/idProduct 2>/dev/null)'"

# WLAN: Samsung's qcacld defers hdd init until the framework WifiHAL writes
# the boot_wlan trigger; UT has no Android framework, so mirror the write
# here (harmless if the node is absent or the driver already initialized).
if [ -w /sys/kernel/boot_wlan/boot_wlan ]; then
    echo 1 > /sys/kernel/boot_wlan/boot_wlan
    echo "ut-usb-retry: boot_wlan trigger written"
    sleep 5
    ip link show wlan0 >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo "ut-usb-retry: wlan0 present" || echo "ut-usb-retry: wlan0 still absent"
else
    echo "ut-usb-retry: no /sys/kernel/boot_wlan node"
fi
exit 0
